                                        "entry_id": "33294cf3-e327-3188-ad64-042787b1c7fe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Without precision or exactness; imprecisely but close to in quantity or amount; approximately."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "612262c7-61c2-40c8-9ec3-466be498042e",
                                                "sense_id": "23fa476f-7c73-39f6-948e-a410002b604b",
                                                "text": "Satanism can be divided, roughly, into two branches: the Luciferians and the Palladists."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6af7cb51-cef4-4b15-9d92-7edaeebcffd6",
                                                "sense_id": "23fa476f-7c73-39f6-948e-a410002b604b",
                                                "text": "Of the roughly 400 emerging infectious diseases that have been identified since 1940, more than 60% are zoonotic: ie they came from animals. Throughout history this has been common."
